{"schema_version":1,"timestamp":"2026-10-11T23:12:42-04:00","cwd":"{NEBULA_PRODUCT_ROOT}","command":"python3 -c 'from pathlib import Path\nroot=Path(\".\")\np=root/\"planning-mds/examples/README.md\"\np.write_text(p.read_text().replace(\"F0023-minimal-entity-360-ui/README.md\", \"F0023-minimal-entity-360/README.md\").replace(\"| One account per organization,\", \"| One current account per organization,\"))\np=root/\"planning-mds/examples/commercial-pc-account/cases.md\"\ntext=p.read_text().replace(\"gives one organization two accounts and fails too.\", \"gives one organization two current accounts and fails too; closed history is covered in EX-PC-021.\")\ntext += \"\"\"\n## EX-PC-020 \u2014 owned policies survive missing or expired insured roles\n\nSynthetic boundary variants of EX-PC-016 remove the Contracting named-insured assignment from GL, or end its party-in-role fact exactly at the snapshot'\"'\"'s valid time. [account-360-contracting.rq](queries/account-360-contracting.rq) still returns GL as `owner`, with an unbound insured-role column (rendered as an empty string by the checker). The other three rows remain unchanged. Policy ownership supplies no evidence of first-named-insured status.\n\nApply those same variants to Contracting'\"'\"'s auto role: auto disappears from the named-on section because Contracting does not own it. The GL, local program and umbrella rows remain. The [regression tests](../../../scripts/validation/tests/test_semantic_examples.py) compare exact rows in all four cases, using the generated valid/known snapshot; the ordinary snapshot still returns the four rows in [expected-results.yaml](expected-results.yaml). Owner: F0012 ownership/role relations and F0023 Account 360, under proposed ADR-0070 sections 3 and 6. These are development examples, not runtime or authorization proof.\n\n## EX-PC-021 \u2014 closed accounts retain history and allow a replacement\n\nThe proposed account lifecycle is a `STATE` fact: `CURRENT` means a non-closed customer relationship, and `CLOSED` preserves a former relationship. This is the teaching vocabulary, not a production CRM status taxonomy. The `accountOrganization` identity link stays `ETERNAL`; the snapshot builder selects status at explicit valid and known times.\n\nIn [account-close-reopen.ttl](boundaries/account-close-reopen.ttl), one organization has an old account that closed on July 1 and a replacement current from July 1. At valid July 5 / known July 11, both accounts and the old account'\"'\"'s policy remain present. [shapes.ttl](shapes.ttl) conforms because only the replacement is current. Changing the old account back to `CURRENT` fails `OneAccountPerOrganizationShape`; missing, unknown or conflicting lifecycle status also fails account completeness. Closure does not transfer policies or delete identity links.\n\nThe temporal regression adds a closure effective July 1, recorded July 10: before July 1 the old account reads `CURRENT`; at July 1 known July 9 it still reads `CURRENT`; at July 1 known July 11 it reads `CLOSED` and the replacement reads `CURRENT`. The exclusive end boundary permits the same-day replacement without overlapping current states. The generated replacement snapshot conforms while retaining both organization links. Historical identity metadata can exist without a known lifecycle reading; an incomplete snapshot cannot certify the uniqueness constraint.\n\nAll these graphs are single-tenant, synthetic examples. Runtime canonical admission must enforce uniqueness across the tenant'\"'\"'s knowledge bases and temporal intervals. Owner: F0012 lifecycle vocabulary/constraints and F0017 account identity; F0023 presents history. Contracts: proposed [ADR-0070 section 2](../../architecture/decisions/ADR-0070-account-party-and-role-model.md#2-accounts), [data model](../../architecture/data-model.md#proposed-party-account-and-role-records-adr-0070), [ontology](ontology.yaml) and [projection mapping](projection-mapping.yaml). No reopening workflow or production delivery is claimed.\n\"\"\"\np.write_text(text)\np=root/\"planning-mds/examples/commercial-pc-account/boundaries/duplicate-organization-account.ttl\"\np.write_text(p.read_text().replace(\"two accounts for one organization\", \"two current accounts for one organization\").replace(\"Each organization has exactly one account in a tenant\", \"Each organization has at most one current account in a tenant\"))\n'","exit_code":0,"artifacts":[],"redactions":[]}
