{"schema_version":1,"timestamp":"2026-10-11T23:16:50-04:00","cwd":"{NEBULA_PRODUCT_ROOT}","command":"python3 -c 'from pathlib import Path\nimport subprocess\nrun=Path(\"planning-mds/operations/evidence/runs/2026-10-11-453de556\")\np=run/\"action-context.md\"\nscope=p.read_text().split(\"# Defect scope\",1)[1]\np.write_text(\"# Action Context\\n\\n## Run Identity\\n\\n- Run: 2026-10-11-453de556\\n- Action: defect-bugfix\\n- Contract version/effective date: 2026-07-11\\n- Mode: clean\\n\\n## Inputs, assumptions and scope\\n\"+scope)\np=run/\"gate-decisions.md\"\np.write_text(\"# Defect decisions\"+p.read_text().split(\"# Defect decisions\",1)[1])\n(run/\"quality-report.md\").write_text(\"\"\"# Quality Engineer report\n\nVerdict: PASS for the two planning-example defects.\n\n## Reproduction and regression mapping\n\n| Case | Evidence | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| EX-PC-020: owned GL, missing/expired insured role | focused-regressions.txt, validation-tests.txt | Retained as owner with empty role, exact other rows preserved |\n| EX-PC-020: non-owned auto, missing/expired insured role | same | Excluded; no ownership or insured status invented |\n| EX-PC-021: closed account plus replacement | same, strict-rdf.txt | Conforms; both identity links and old policy ownership preserved |\n| EX-PC-021: two current accounts | same | Rejected by OneAccountPerOrganizationShape |\n| EX-PC-021: missing/unknown/conflicting status | same | Rejected at accountStatus |\n| EX-PC-021: before/at closure, before/after recorded closure | temporal-final.txt | Old status and replacement selected by both timelines; post-closure graph conforms |\n\nArtifacts above live in artifacts/test-results/. reproduction.txt captures the original three failures and two passing controls. focused-regressions.txt contains 12 passes. validation-tests.txt contains all 63 validation tests passing (51 prior tests plus 12 added cases). temporal-final.txt rechecks the four temporal cases after strengthening replacement-slot identity and retained-link assertions.\n\n## Validation matrix\n\n- Strict RDF: PASS, Python 3.12.13, rdflib 7.1.4, pyshacl 0.30.1, owlrl 7.1.4.\n- Full product lifecycle: all four gates PASS in lifecycle-venv.txt: KG integrity, KG reproducibility, semantic examples, semantic RDF. An initial lifecycle command used system Python for its child commands and skipped optional RDF; lifecycle.txt preserves that attempt. The repeat explicitly prepended the product virtual environment and executed RDF successfully.\n- Project and F0001 planning readiness: PASS with no findings; commands.log records invocations.\n- Trackers: PASS with zero errors/warnings (trackers.txt).\n- Stories: PASS (stories.txt); heuristics warn on existing unchanged story independence/value wording.\n- KG drift/freshness: PASS; generated coverage metadata refreshed. Existing unused-edge and compile name-similarity warnings remain outside the changed semantics.\n- git diff --check: PASS.\n\n## Scope limits\n\nThese are synthetic development examples outside the frozen holdout. No production application, database, UI, authorization code or deployment changes were made, so runtime integration/E2E, security scans and runtime coverage measurement are not applicable (QE scope decision). No coverage percentage, independent-agent signoff, feature completion, production readiness or ADR acceptance is claimed. Python dependency deprecation warnings do not fail the executed tests.\n\"\"\")\nchanged=subprocess.check_output([\"git\",\"diff\",\"--name-only\"],text=True).splitlines()\nnew=\"planning-mds/examples/commercial-pc-account/boundaries/account-close-reopen.ttl\"\n(run/\"artifact-trace.md\").write_text(\"\"\"# Artifact trace\n\n## Artifacts read\n\n- Framework: agents/ROUTER.md, agents/agent-map.yaml, architect/backend-developer/quality-engineer SKILL.md, defect-bugfix action/spec/generated prompt, AGENT-USE.md, AGENT-OPS.md, PROJECT-EXTENSIONS.md, selected data-modeling and architecture-best-practices guidance.\n- Product: .agentignore, .nebula-project.yaml, BLUEPRINT.md, docs/agent-instructions.md, ADR-0070, data-model.md, glossary.md, semantic example index and full relevant commercial bundle, validation scripts/tests, account KG source and example bindings, registry and lifecycle configuration.\n- Project context loader ran successfully for defect-bugfix with the explicit absolute product root.\n\n## Artifacts created or updated\n\n\"\"\"+ \"\\n\".join(\"- \"+p for p in changed+[new]) + \"\"\"\n\n## Generated evidence\n\n- This run'\"'\"'s base files plus architect-analysis.md, backend-fix-report.md and quality-report.md.\n- D0\u2013D5 runner output under artifacts/, gate-state.json and lifecycle-gates.log.\n- Test output under artifacts/test-results/; exact executed commands and exit codes in commands.log.\n- Snapshot Turtle/JSON-LD/lineage index regenerated with build_commercial_pc_snapshot.py; release digests refreshed.\n- Authored KG sources compiled with scripts/kg/compile.py; coverage report generated by validate.py, never manually edited.\n\n## Run Environment\n\nCodex exercised the three roles sequentially in the shared workspace. No separate reviewers or sub-agents were claimed. Absolute framework/product paths in command records bind the sibling repositories explicitly. Framework working tree remains clean. The product virtual environment provides RDF dependencies; system Python does not. The 2026-10-11 local run crosses 2026-10-12 UTC in generated freshness metadata.\n\n## Diagnostics and omissions\n\nPre-run discovery initially tried git status from the workspace parent (not a repository), guessed an ADR filename, and later omitted --file for a KG blast lookup; exact paths/flags corrected these diagnostics. A guessed schema-node path was absent; the existing account node and binding source were used instead. The first D0 output capture used a relative path resolved outside the product root and was rejected before gate execution (exit 2); an absolute capture path succeeded. These command setup issues were not validator defects or product failures.\n\nThe base-file scaffolder included example feature G0\u2013G8 rows and TODOs; they were replaced with the actual D0\u2013D5 defect record before closeout. No feature evidence manifest, latest-run pointer, signoff ledger or feature-folder writes were produced. All actual defects and required checks are resolved. Broader runtime delivery and ADR proof gates remain with their existing owners.\n\"\"\")\n(run/\"README.md\").write_text(\"\"\"# ADR-0070 example defect repair \u2014 2026-10-11-453de556\n\n## Run Summary\n\nArchitect-led defect-bugfix action, with Backend Developer and Quality Engineer roles exercised sequentially by Codex. Account 360 now includes owned policies independently of named-insured roles. Dated account lifecycle distinguishes CURRENT and CLOSED, so retained closed history allows a replacement while two current accounts still fail validation. ADR, data model, glossary, examples and generated KG projections agree.\n\n## Status\n\nImplementation and validation complete; final Architect closeout recorded in gate-decisions.md. Lifecycle Authority = none. ADR-0070 remains Proposed. This is a base defect run, not feature completion evidence.\n\n## Evidence Index\n\n- [Architect analysis](architect-analysis.md): root cause, governing intent and implementation handoff.\n- [Backend fix report](backend-fix-report.md): executable example changes.\n- [Quality report](quality-report.md): boundary coverage and validation matrix.\n- [Action context](action-context.md), [artifact trace](artifact-trace.md), [gate decisions](gate-decisions.md).\n- commands.log and lifecycle-gates.log; runner outputs and test results under artifacts/.\n\n## Validation Summary\n\nThree failing reproduction cases became passing regressions. All 63 validation tests pass, including 12 new cases. Strict RDF and all four product lifecycle gates pass with RDF actually executed. Planning readiness, tracker and story checks pass. KG source/projection reproducibility and freshness checks pass. Existing dependency/heuristic warnings are recorded in quality-report.md.\n\n## Open Follow-ups\n\nNone for the two reviewed defects. Production account lifecycle enforcement and Account 360 delivery remain with F0012/F0017/F0023 under the existing Proposed ADR; no production acceptance or feature status was advanced.\n\"\"\")\n'","exit_code":0,"artifacts":[],"redactions":[]}
